Subject: [PATCH] Gate /api/progress behind requireStaff, as /api/pt-os already
 is
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This router was missed when that gate went in, and the gap is the same one,
with the same cause written in the pt-os comment: read routes were auth-only,
harmless only for as long as no account held the `member` role.

Every GET here takes an OPTIONAL client_id — omit it and you get the whole
organisation's rows. Nine routes behave that way: assessments, goals,
weekly-checkins, strength-logs, progress-photos, lifestyle, nutrition, mobility
and posture. tenantScope() keeps that inside one studio, which is the boundary
that matters for tenancy, so this is not a cross-tenant leak. But a `member`
account created by a client login carries that studio's organization_id, so
`auth` alone let a client call GET /api/progress/assessments with no client_id
and read every other client's body composition, health notes and trainer notes
in their own gym.

A client's own progress is served by /api/me, which scopes to the caller.

The test asserts the MOUNT rather than the handlers, because the mount is where
the fix lives and where a refactor would silently drop it — and spells out the
failing shape so a reviewer can see what regressed if it goes red.

BEFORE MERGING: confirm no client-facing frontend screen calls /api/progress
directly. This session could read the backend but not the frontend, so that one
could not be checked here. If a client screen does use it, the route it wants is
under /api/me.

